 "_readme": "Maintainable list of sources harvested by scripts/harvest_feeds.py. Add an entry, commit, and the next run picks it up. 'feed' is optional: if blank or broken, the harvester tries RSS/Atom autodiscovery on 'url'. For YouTube give 'youtube' as a handle (@name) or channel id (UC...). For Bluesky give 'bluesky' as a handle. Platforms without public feeds (LinkedIn, Instagram, X) are listed with 'feed': null and appear as links only. 'status' fields are written by the harvester; do not edit by hand. Sites without a feed are scraped: the harvester reads the listing page ('scrape_url', default 'url'), keeps article links (optionally only those matching the regex 'link_pattern'), then reads each article's title, description and date. Set 'scrape': false to turn scraping off for a source.",
